Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 20:23:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07572/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-WMTE-5827 results:
 reactive-filter loop honest negative, real diagnosis

Real 3-game empirical test (sc25, lf52, bp35 -- the worst live/oracle-gap
games from exp5727's full-registry sweep) of the verifier-filtered
reactive loop vs the standing induce-then-plan mechanism. Clean runs on
all three (0 crashes, adversarial_verify 0-flagged), filter mechanism
genuinely active every round (frame_change_rejections 518/596/600) --
but levels_gained=0 on all three, matching the induce-then-plan baseline
exactly.

Diagnosed WHY, not just that it failed (ops/verifier_gaps.md
GAP-ARC-REACTIVE-FILTER-MYOPIC): the filter's two signals (dead-end
rejection, change-prediction) are both purely local/single-step: neither
encodes direction toward a distant goal, and these games need deep,
narrow winning sequences with no intermediate reward a local filter can
climb. This is a genuinely different failure mode from the induction-
quality gap, not a restatement of it -- the reactive loop's per-step
correctness is real, but it gave up the multi-step lookahead the (also
failing) induce-then-plan architecture was trying to provide. Neither
architecture alone combines reliable per-step signal with goal-directed
search; that combination is the real missing capability, and the
concrete next candidates (n-step rollout using the filter as step-
evaluator, or a general learned goal-progress signal) are logged.

